{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1792371150180491650,"compiled_state":{"alias":"glandulous-minor-aurochs","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5e267d78430c70d214083c50893d8bfde76a1fa98caac0541e903d6740c37bbb","event_uuid":"a9cf0eda-17b0-4af2-8982-b6f97d832a9a","position":{"commit_sha":"60a0f8206127b77172e23a3d63f47d5b121ab56c","position":"1792371123039919817-a9cf0eda-17b0-4af2-8982-b6f97d832a9a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"79cdc53a6af207240293c5b1ed8ea0285cd2cd8c6c8f9eaaaee0c8b12acbcdc7","event_uuid":"17d81496-adc2-4eae-b641-71b7a05df63a","position":{"commit_sha":"beab53a7049aa12166b6f600b45482a5ab3e6271","position":"1792371150180491649-17d81496-adc2-4eae-b641-71b7a05df63a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1792371123039919817,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"17d81496-adc2-4eae-b641-71b7a05df63a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3b27-8f4b-90bd-44b2"}],"description":"## Problem\n\nThe MCP server reviews plan material from its own tickets clone. An edit made in another\nclone (local CLI or library) reaches that clone only through `reads.ensure_fresh`\n(`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`), a best-effort `git fetch` throttled to once per\n60 s by a `/tmp/.ticket-sync-<md5>` marker. `collect_plan_relation_snapshot` (review start)\nand the under-lock re-collect in `generation.sign_manifest` both go through that throttle.\n\nSo a review started, or signed, within 60 s of the server's previous fetch can pin a\ndescription that is already superseded on `origin`. The under-lock re-check compares against\nthe same lagging clone, so it does not catch this. A claim through the same server inside the\nsame window would also see the lagging clone.\n\nSplit from next-embattled-geese (3b27-8f4b), which fixes the separate dedup-attach window.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Code path read on origin/main 3beb7e4ad23: `tracker_head_sha` -> `ticket_reads.ensure_fresh`\n  -> throttle check `marker_age < 60: return`.\n- Not yet reproduced end to end; needs two clones sharing one origin.\n\n## Approach to decide in plan review\n\nBypass the throttle (forced fetch + reconverge) for the gate's own material reads at review\nstart and before taking the signing lock, without fetching while the store lock is held.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Two-clone test: edit in clone A and push; within 60 s of clone B's last fetch, a review\n  started on B pins A's edited description.\n- [ ] Signing on B refuses when A's edit lands on origin during the run.\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit -k cross_clone_freshness -q\n```","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"36d1-9578-d4b3-48c9","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP plan review can read and sign a tickets clone up to 60 s behind origin after a cross-clone edit","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a9cf0eda-17b0-4af2-8982-b6f97d832a9a","17d81496-adc2-4eae-b641-71b7a05df63a"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792371150180491650,"uuid":"caa9dcd4-3065-4b86-b44a-f97ccf058383"}